.Dd September 11, 2026
.Dt DWLM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dwlm
.Nd wlroots compositor with a Niri-style scroll workspace
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl s Ar startup command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a Wayland compositor based on wlroots, forked from
.Xr dwl 1 .
.Pp
Besides the classic dwm layouts, it ships a horizontal
.Em scroll
layout: windows live in columns on an infinite strip, and the viewport
follows the focused column with an animated pan, in the style of Niri.
.Pp
When given the
.Fl v
option,
.Nm
prints its logo, name and version to standard error and exits unsuccessfully.
.Pp
When given the
.Fl d
option,
.Nm
enables full wlroots logging, including debug information.
.Pp
When given the
.Fl s
option,
.Nm
starts a shell process running
.Ar command
when starting.
When stopping, it sends
.Dv SIGTERM
to the child process and waits for it to exit.
.Pp
.Nm
exposes the
.Sy zwlr_foreign_toplevel_manager_v1
protocol so status bars and shell clients can track windows (title, app_id,
activated/maximized/fullscreen state, output placement and close/activate
requests).  XWayland clients are supported when built with
.Dv XWAYLAND .
.Pp
Users are encouraged to customize
.Nm
by editing the sources, in particular
.Pa src/config.def.h
(writes to a local
.Pa src/config.h
are compiled in).  Runtime scroll parameters, window rules and colors can
also be tweaked from a TOML configuration file which is re-applied live on
.Dv SIGHUP
(no restart needed); see
.Pa \(ti/.config/dwlm/config.toml
and
.Pa src/config_runtime.c .
.Pp
In the keybindings below Demlo (Mod) is the Super/Logo key:
.Bl -tag -width 20n -offset indent -compact
.It Ic Mod-P
Spawn
.Nm wmenu-run .
.It Ic Mod-Return , Mod-Shift-Return
Spawn
.Nm foot .
.It Ic Mod-H/L , Mod-Left/Right
Focus column left/right in scroll mode.
.It Ic Mod-J/K , Mod-Up/Down
Focus the window below/above in the column (stack).
.It Ic Mod-Shift-H/L
Move the focused column left/right on the strip.
.It Ic Mod-Home/End
Focus the first/last column.
.It Ic Mod-Ctrl-Home/End
Move the focused column to the first/last position.
.It Ic Mod-Shift-V
Cycle the column width preset (33/50/67 percent).
.It Ic Mod-minus/equal
Shrink/grow the column width (master factor while tiling).
.It Ic Mod-C
Center the focused column in the viewport.
.It Ic Mod-R , Mod-Shift-R
Toggle resize (column) mode.
.It Ic Mod-bracketleft
Consume the focused window into the column to its left.
.It Ic Mod-bracketright
Expel the focused window into a column of its own.
.It Ic Mod-A
Toggle the floating state of the focused window.
.It Ic Mod-E
Toggle fullscreen.
.It Ic Mod-Q
Close the focused window.
.It Ic Mod-T / Mod-F
Switch to tile / floating layout.
.It Ic Mod-Shift-M
Switch to monocle layout.
.It Ic Mod-Shift-S
Switch to scroll layout.
.It Ic Mod-Space
Switch to the previous layout.
.It Ic Mod-M
Toggle maximized on the focused window.
.It Ic Mod-1\(en9
View workspace N.
.It Ic Mod-Ctrl-1\(en9
Toggle workspace N in the view.
.It Ic Mod-Shift-exclam\(enparenleft
Tag/untag the focused window to workspace N.
.It Ic Mod-Ctrl-Shift-exclam\(enparenleft
Toggle workspace N on the focused window.
.It Ic Mod-Alt-1\(en9
Focus the Nth column of the strip (workspace N while tiling).
.It Ic Mod-0
View all workspaces.
.It Ic Mod-Shift-parenright
Tag the focused window to all workspaces.
.It Ic Mod-comma/period
Focus previous/next monitor.
.It Ic Mod-Shift-less/greater
Move the focused column to the previous/next monitor.
.It Ic Mod-Shift-E
Quit
.Nm .
.El
.Pp
Mouse bindings:
.Bl -tag -width 20n -offset indent -compact
.It Ic Mod-button1
Drag a floating window (or move a column).
.It Ic Mod-button3
Resize a floating window (or a column).
.It Ic Mod-button2
Toggle floating state.
.El
.Pp
These might differ depending on your keyboard layout.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
These environment variables are used by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
A directory where temporary user files, such as the Wayland socket,
are stored.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_DIR
A directory containing configuration of various programs and
libraries, including libxkbcommon.
.It Ev DISPLAY , WAYLAND_DISPLAY , WAYLAND_SOCKET
Tell how to connect to an underlying X11 or Wayland server.
.It Ev WLR_*
Various variables specific to wlroots.
.It Ev XKB_* , XLOCALEDIR , XCOMPOSEFILE
Various variables specific to libxkbcommon.
.It Ev XCURSOR_PATH
List of directories to search for XCursor themes in.
.El
.Pp
These are set by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width WAYLAND_DISPLAY
.It Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Tell how to connect to
.Nm .
.It Ev DISPLAY
If using
.Nm Xwayland ,
tell how to connect to the
.Nm Xwayland
server.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width src/config.def.h
.It Pa src/config.def.h
Default compile-time configuration and keybindings.
.It Pa src/config_runtime.c
TOML runtime configuration of scroll parameters, window rules and colors.
.It Pa \(ti/.config/dwlm/config.toml
Optional TOML overlay, re-applied live on
.Dv SIGHUP :
keys
.Ar borderpx , Ar corner_radius , Ar gap , Ar outer_gap , Ar width_min ,
.Ar width_max , Ar presets , Ar mouse_scroll , Ar pixels_per_notch ,
.Ar continuous_speed , Ar anim_ms , Ar anim_ease ,
.Ar root / Ar border / Ar focus / Ar urgent
colors and
.Ar [rules.N]
window rules.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start
.Nm
with a terminal and a bar shell client:
.Dl dwlm -s "foot"
.Pp
Change the focus ring to a red 2 px border, drop the gap and let Calculator
float, then reload live:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cat \(aq\(aq \(ti/.config/dwlm/config.toml
[general]
borderpx       = 2
gap            = 4
[colors]
focus          = "#ff6666"
[rules.1]
app_id         = "calc"
isfloating     = true
\(aq\(aq
kill -HUP "$(pgrep dwlm)"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr foot 1 ,
.Xr wmenu 1 ,
.Xr dwl 1 ,
.Xr dwm 1 ,
.Xr xkeyboard-config 7 ,
.Xr niri 1
.Sh CAVEATS
The child process's standard input is connected with a pipe to
.Nm .
If the child process neither reads from the pipe nor closes its
standard input,
.Nm
will freeze after a while due to it blocking when writing to the full
pipe buffer.
.Sh BUGS
All of them.